WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.834
Russian President

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.535
Vladimir Putin says that his country

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.637
is going through a difficult time

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.772
as Ukrainian forces

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.774
claim success on the battlefield.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:08.575
Putin's admission

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.876
came during his Russia day

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.144
address to the nation.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:11.478
Ukraine's

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.113
military says that it has made gains

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.314
in the southeast,

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.383
recapturing three front line villages,

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.851
and they continue to make advances

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.119
on several fronts.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:19.652
Joining me now

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:20.687
to discuss is Lieutenant

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.988
General Mark Hertling,

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.423
a CNN military analyst.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.657
General, welcome to the program.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.125
Good morning.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.760
So I want to start there with that

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.261
new CNN reporting

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.063
that we are seeing at Vance's long

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:30.830
certain areas

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.766
of the border, Donetsk, for example,

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:33.800
zapping Russia.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.468
What do you make of that?

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:39.506
These are still not the main attack,

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.240
in my view,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.741
or how this is still

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:45.045
sort of the looking for places to attack

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:46.312
you know,

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.548
this is the very early stages of

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.382
this offensive.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.551
And whenever you have an early stage,

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.352
what you're doing

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.020
is looking for an advantage

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.688
and attempting to move the enemy

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.457
forces around.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.625
Ukraine is doing that.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.093
They are probing in a very

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.628
a variety of direction.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.629
The American public

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:03.363
all knows

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.697
now the military terms

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.366
of shaping operations

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.368
and probing and reconnaissance in force.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.537
That's what they're continuing to do.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.605
So you're seeing some tough fighting.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.775
Ukraine has entered into the first two

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:19.179
of four complex obstacle belts,

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.880
and they are having great success

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.949
in liberating small villages.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.517
But we're going to see what's

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.952
going to happen next.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.121
And I'll introduce you to two new phrases

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.789
that we'll start using soon.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.291
And that's main attack

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.892
and supporting attacks.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.594
That's what Ukraine will eventually do

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.662
when they find out

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.931
the best places to employ their reserves.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.333
General, as you say, early days

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.267
in this counteroffensive.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.068
We're about one weekend,

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.336
but CNN is reporting that

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.038
at least according to an open source,

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.372
Intel Agence Analysis

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.641
that Ukraine has has lost 16

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.477
of its armored vehicles from the U.S.

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:53.680
It's about 15% of the 109 that the U.S.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.582
had provided at this stage.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:56.449
In the counter-offensive

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.884
early days, as you say.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.818
What do you think about

00:01:58.818 --> 00:01:59.853
that rate of loss there

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.455
When you're

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:05.492
whenever a force goes into an obstacle

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.392
belt, like you're

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.994
seeing Russia has built

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.696
over the last seven months,

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.631
you're going to lose vehicles

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.066
you're going to

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:14.434
they're going to get destroyed.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.435
Truthfully, now,

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:15.802
when we're

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.403
talking about armored vehicles,

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.373
we don't know what type of each

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.975
kinds of armor vehicles

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.810
are these lethal tanks that they've lost,

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.545
are they Bradley fighting vehicles

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.513
or are they Strykers

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.680
or are they high marks?

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.548
We don't know.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:31.384
Ukraine is doing a very good job in terms

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.520
of keeping operational security.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.687
But truthfully,

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.389
I think everyone's getting excited

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.525
about the fact that Russia has shown

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.759
a couple of pictures

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.895
of what they claim are destroyed

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:43.429
Ukrainian vehicles.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.232
But as heartless as this sounds.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.934
That is to be expected

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.302
in the kind of operations

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.870
Ukraine is conducted

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.905
They're on the offensive

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.773
against a tough defensive belt.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.241
So you're going to lose some vehicles

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.009
and unfortunately,

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.178
you're going to have casualties as well.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:59.479
General, what do you make of Putin

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:00.413
saying that this is a

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.248
difficult time for Russia

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.052
Yeah, that's fascinating.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.954
When I heard that report this morning,

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:10.623
he has increasingly admitted

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.692
some of the challenges

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.094
that Russia is experiencing now.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.130
Part of that is to generate

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.665
additional support

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.733
from the Russian Russian people

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:24.170
as he attempts to mobilize more forces or

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.606
manufacture more vehicles,

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:29.042
more ammunition and do different things.

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.044
So when he says it's a difficult

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.446
time, he's basically signaling

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.248
I believe, to the Russian people

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.517
that we have to step up the operations

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.751
and that there will be

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.286
more pain and suffering,

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.689
whether it's in return

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.257
injured and killed

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:45.825
soldiers, Russian soldiers

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.560
or banks shutting down

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.462
or less goods on the market

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.931
or less opportunities for Russian people

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:52.599
to do that.

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:53.233
Kind of things

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.434
that they're used to doing.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.402
So all of those things are signals

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.837
from a politician

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.073
to basically prepare for more losses

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.508
and more damages to his government.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.410
Really fascinating statement now.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.878
15 months into the war.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.080
General, great to have you today.

